name lgb-designate-1
timeout 160

# A GUIDED BOMB BINDS ITS SHOOTER. doc/air-to-ground.md §3.2.
#
# An LGB is a SEMI-ACTIVE weapon whose illuminator is the shooter — not an analogy but the same
# mechanism the R-27R already runs, at a different wavelength: the designation travels the SAME
# published channel the midcourse uplink does (FBUnitSignature, read by the round's own comms slot),
# and the round has no idea where the point is except that somebody is holding it.
#
# The viper releases at 5.6 km from 4 000 m, CCRP, against a briefed steerpoint. The ballistic error at
# release is over a kilometre; the kit flies it down to a MEASURED 52.78 m — OUTSIDE the documented
# Paveway II CEP band of 6-9 m [T4], which is the number this file is checked against and which is NOT
# a setting: the miss is whatever the pursuit law produces.
#
# THIS FILE IS RED AND STAYS RED, and the reason is worth more than the green was.
# The 3.9 m this file used to report was never a property of the weapon. The laser spot's ELEVATION is
# the CCRP impact plane, and that plane used to be the ground under the SHOOTER instead of under the
# TARGET (doc/air-to-ground.md `C30`; the same defect that made mods/f22 c01m08 miss by 230 m). Here the
# shooter sits 30.45 m above the target, so the spot hung 30.45 m in the air, the still-descending round
# crossed the real surface further downrange, and one error cancelled the other to within 2 m.
# MEASURED as a characteristic curve (temporary offset on the spot elevation, reverted):
#     +30.45 m of spot error -> aimErrM  2.33 m      (what this file used to report)
#     +15.00 m               -> aimErrM 28.01 m
#      0     m, correct      -> aimErrM 52.78 m
# ~1.66 m of miss per metre of spot error, zero crossing at +31.8 m. THE DEFECT THIS FILE NOW SHOWS IS
# THE GUIDANCE: the GBU-12's bang-bang pursuit law runs out of authority ~53 m short of a correctly
# designated spot. Do not relax the bound and do not move the geometry — repair the law.
#
# THE LAW IS NOT PROPORTIONAL NAVIGATION and must not be: the CCG's canards are bang-bang, so the round
# aligns its velocity vector with the instantaneous line of sight and trails the fins when aligned. It
# therefore CHASES the spot and pays for the chase in energy, at a measured ~2.6 g of authority against
# a missile's 25 g command ceiling (doc/air-to-ground.md §Knowledge 4).
#
# THE SHOOTER IS HELD ON THE RUN-IN by its own SMS: while `FBStoresBlock::Designating` is true the pilot
# does not start the egress turn. That is one instrument read and no new phase.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log      `missile SEEKER_ACTIVE ... mode="semi-active laser"`, NO `missile
#                   ILLUMINATION_LOST` anywhere, and `stores DELIVERY ... aimErrM` — today 52.78 m
#   UNIT_RESULT     bunker DESTROYED (a soft target still dies at 53 m; the CEP claim is what fails)
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 is not the measurement. The MEASUREMENT is `aimErrM` on the `stores DELIVERY`
# line against the published 6-9 m band, and `UNIT_RESULT unit=bunker result=DESTROYED`. The band is
# NOT met and the file is honest about it. Read as the first of three: lgb-lase-broken.fbm and
# lgb-lase-restored.fbm move ONE line each.

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.90000 6.98000 4000 90.0 250
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set store 3 gbu12
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task route
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set brief_release_s 3
  wp 46.90000 7.05000 4000 250
  wp 46.90000 7.30000 4000 250
  objective survive

unit bunker
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 46.90000 7.05000 ground 90.0 0
